{:db/id "answer-field-d09acdef-394b-56b7-aede-21eb94c695dd" :answer-field/id #uuid "d09acdef-394b-56b7-aede-21eb94c695dd" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-0e536d67-208f-5109-860d-8ce8e8456549" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0e536d67-208f-5109-860d-8ce8e8456549" "answer-125c2c98-2434-5932-a480-2510a1b6f6d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e536d67-208f-5109-860d-8ce8e8456549" :answer/id #uuid "0e536d67-208f-5109-860d-8ce8e8456549" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a stable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-125c2c98-2434-5932-a480-2510a1b6f6d9" :answer/id #uuid "125c2c98-2434-5932-a480-2510a1b6f6d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an unstable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6382c6a6-f666-5da1-8304-c0b7d94b708d" :answer-field/id #uuid "6382c6a6-f666-5da1-8304-c0b7d94b708d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-61ca4b5b-b2d8-5291-94f1-c7eb2d49d57c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0adbae6f-09ad-5e85-adc2-3211170c6c66" "answer-61ca4b5b-b2d8-5291-94f1-c7eb2d49d57c" "answer-15eece98-8f78-5bc6-9ed2-aea0eb111e1c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0adbae6f-09ad-5e85-adc2-3211170c6c66" :answer/id #uuid "0adbae6f-09ad-5e85-adc2-3211170c6c66" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a saddle point" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61ca4b5b-b2d8-5291-94f1-c7eb2d49d57c" :answer/id #uuid "61ca4b5b-b2d8-5291-94f1-c7eb2d49d57c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a stable node (sink)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15eece98-8f78-5bc6-9ed2-aea0eb111e1c" :answer/id #uuid "15eece98-8f78-5bc6-9ed2-aea0eb111e1c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an unstable node (source)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d325e43f-35f1-5542-8db8-397925f79316" :question/id #uuid "d325e43f-35f1-5542-8db8-397925f79316" :question/math-academy-id "q-333656" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)+2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t)+2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[2,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options below regarding the given system.\n\n$\\,$\n$y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ is {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-2}} is {{field-3}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=\\frac{1}{2}x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable node (source)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/e5/e5c236defa66a00f12cd338ed0012cf91e4d7c15aa4865fc2b1edf5b0e2ea1da.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-067d8b08-6895-5be5-a9f6-a2b1e3667c9